<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`<<~ ahu #/slot>>` … `<<~/ahu>>` bounds a worksite scope and addresses a child-slot record at `parentUri#/slot`.

''One slot, one address.'' A slot spelled `#a` or `#/a` resolves to `#/a` under the meme root, and to `#/a/c` under the child `#/a` — the fragment never repeats its `#`. The deserializer mints the record's title by that same law.

The declaration rides in `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/sigil-ahu.tid`, which carries the open and close patterns TW5 matches (`lar-open-pattern`, `lar-close-pattern`) and the `\widget ~ahu(slot uri p1)` body. The widget resolves the child URI, then hands the render to a TEMPLATE, never to a class.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/template-cascade>>

!! The Template Cascade

The widget picks its template by filter, and falls back to the shipped default only when the cascade finds nothing:

```
[all[shadows+tiddlers]tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/ahu-template]!is[draft]]
  :map:flat[subfilter{!!text}]
  +[first[]else[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/templates/ahu/html]]
```

A wiki overrides the render by tagging its own pointer tiddler `lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/ahu-template`; the shipped pointer names `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/templates/ahu/html`.

''Two postures, two cascades.'' `~kahea~ahu` picks the ahu cascade (live child-slot transclusion); `~aka~ahu` picks the aka cascade (frozen projection read of the same child). Posture lives in the cascade, never in sigil dispatch. `lar-sigil.ts` routes the compound form `name="kahea~ahu", p1=slot`.

Live wiki parent tiddlers hold the space form `<<~ kahea ahu #slot>>`, which reads under a HUD.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/slot-states>>

!! Four Slot States

A section with nothing under it says the same nothing for three different facts, so the template names which fact it met. It stamps `data-slot-state` on the `<section>` and mirrors it into the class as `lar-ahu-<state>`:

| State | The reading that produces it | What it means |
|---|---|---|
| `unresolved` | `[is[missing]]` — no record stands at the child's address | a member left alone and the root's call stayed; the house keeps the pointer and marks it dead, never inventing bytes |
| `arriving` | a record stands, holding no `text` field | the poll lands a group skinny in one batch and fattens it one title at a time — this window, named |
| `empty` | a record stands, its text empty | the author wrote nothing, which counts as a fact too |
| `filled` | everything else | the body transcludes in block mode |

''One reading tells the first two apart:'' an arriving child HAS a record and a dead one does not.

<<~/ahu>>

